kobold-miner contains open-source code. This file lists those parts and gives the license texts they ask to be
shipped with the program. LICENSE-APACHE holds the Apache License 2.0.

1. BoundHash
   kobold-miner's CPU and GPU BoundHash code follows BOUND's src/core/boundhash.cpp
   (https://github.com/Sonic-Bound/Bound, v1.1.0). MIT License, text in section A.

2. NEB
   NEB mining uses the NEB node's crates neb-pow (with its C reference code), neb-work, neb-block, neb-chain,
   neb-codec and neb-difficulty (https://github.com/SilasEigen/neb, v1.0.4), Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE-APACHE).
   kobold-miner's GPU screening kernel implements NEB's BLAKE3 and ChaCha8 steps from NEB's spec/shares.md.

3. Rust crates under the Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE-APACHE)
   These crates offer a choice of licenses; kobold-miner uses them under the Apache License 2.0:
   the Rust standard library, arrayvec, base64ct, blake3, block-buffer, cfg-if, const-oid, constant_time_eq,
   cpufeatures, crypto-common, der, digest, ed25519, getrandom, hybrid-array, itoa, libc, pkcs8, rand_core, serde,
   serde_core, serde_json, sha2, signature, spki, typenum, windows-link, zeroize.
   memchr is used under the Unlicense (public domain).

4. Rust crates under other licenses, texts below
   - curve25519-dalek 4.1.3 and 5.0.0: BSD-3-Clause (section B)
   - ed25519-dalek 2.2.0 and 3.0.0: BSD-3-Clause (section C)
   - subtle 2.6.1: BSD-3-Clause (section D)
   - generic-array 0.14.7: MIT (section E)
   - zmij 1.0.23 (David Tolnay): MIT (section F)
   - libloading 0.8.9: ISC (section G)

5. Windows build
   The Windows program also contains start-up code from the MinGW-w64 runtime (public domain and Zope Public
   License 2.1, https://www.mingw-w64.org) and GCC's runtime library (GPL with the GCC Runtime Library Exception).


